<title>USA: Shuffle Master buys Yoseloff game library.</title>
<headline>Shuffle Master buys Yoseloff game library.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shuffle Master Inc said Monday it purchased an extensive library of proprietary games from Mark Yoseloff, and it will soon begin efforts to commercialize those games.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed. The library includes games developed by Yoseloff.</p>
<p>The company, a supplier of shuffler systems and video games to the casino and gaming industry, also said it signed a five-year employment agreement with Yoseloff, who will develop games with Shuffle Master's new games division.</p>
<p>Shuffle Master will own all future games developed by Yoseloff while he works for the company.</p>
<p>		((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
